    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Sol Ring costs {1}, which requires tapping one of the three lands. Playing a land first (Forest or Grand Coliseum) would give o4-mini 4 lands total after casting Sol Ring, leaving more mana available for future turns. By casting Sol Ring before playing a land, they still have 3 lands + Sol Ring, but they miss the opportunity to have the land drop this turn if they forget or if something prevents it later. More importantly, the sequencing is slightly off - you should always play your land first before casting spells to maximize available mana. However, since they can still play a land after casting Sol Ring in the same main phase, this is a very minor sequencing concern. The real question is which land to play: Forest is likely better than Grand Coliseum since it enters untapped and provides green mana needed for several cards in hand (Wild Beastmaster, Shamanic Revelation, Clan Defiance, Abzan Charm). But casting Sol Ring before the land drop doesn't lose anything concrete since they can still play the land afterward.",
