    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem2.5Flash cast Sigiled Paladin before combat. With no other creatures on board, attacking isn't relevant right now, but more importantly, casting the creature before combat telegraphs information and doesn't leverage any combat tricks. However, the bigger sequencing issue is that Sigiled Paladin should ideally be cast after playing a land (Island or Plains from hand) to keep options open, though in this case it doesn't matter much since the Paladin costs WW which is already available. The real concern is casting a creature into Haiku4.5's open board with Garna/Xathrid Necromancer when Gem2.5Flash has Hinder in hand - casting the Paladin before combat means if an opponent does something during combat, mana is now more constrained. Additionally, with Darksteel Plate and Banshee's Blade both unequipped and a new creature entering, the sequencing of play land first (to have more mana available for equipping) would have been slightly better.",
