    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Haiku4.5 equipped Heirloom Blade to a Zombie Token instead of Frontier Warmonger. Frontier Warmonger is already a 7/5 (likely already equipped or buffed), but Heirloom Blade gives +3/+1 and its death trigger finds a creature sharing a type. Frontier Warmonger is a Human Warrior - if it dies with Heirloom Blade, you'd search for another Human (relevant given Jirina Kudro commander and Human tribal deck). A Zombie Token dying with Heirloom Blade would search for a Zombie, and there are likely no Zombie creatures in the deck to find. The +3/+1 stats also matter more on the 4/4 Warmonger (making it a 10/6 threat) than on a 2/2 Zombie Token (making it 5/3). The Warmonger with its menace-granting ability is the premium threat that benefits most from both the stats and the death trigger.",
      "action_taken": "Equipped Heirloom Blade to a 2/2 Zombie Token",
      "better_line": "Equip Heirloom Blade to Frontier Warmonger for +3/+1 on the biggest threat and a meaningful death trigger that could find another Human creature from the deck",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 314,
      "player": "Haiku4.5",
      "decision_index": 453,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Unclaimed Territory's second ability produces mana that can only be spent to cast creature spells of the chosen type. Haiku4.5 chose this option but used the mana for Heirloom Blade's equip cost, which is an activated ability, not casting a creature spell. The colorless mana option (option 1) has no spending restriction and would be the correct choice for paying equip costs.",
      "action_taken": "Chose Unclaimed Territory's second ability (colored mana restricted to creature spells) to pay for Heirloom Blade's equip cost",
      "better_line": "Choose option 1 ({T}: Add {C}) which has no spending restriction and can legally pay for any cost including equip",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 314,
      "player": "Haiku4.5",
      "decision_index": 453,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Haiku4.5 attempted to activate Heirloom Blade's Equip ability with no creatures on the battlefield. All creatures are in the graveyard. This activation either fails or wastes mana on an impossible action.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to activate Heirloom Blade — Equip {1} with no creatures to equip.",
      "better_line": "Play Plains from hand first (land drop), then pass since there are no creatures to equip. The only productive action available is playing the Plains.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 314,
      "player": "Haiku4.5",
      "decision_index": 453,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Equipped Heirloom Blade to a Zombie Token instead of Frontier Warmonger. Zombie Tokens are token creatures that share the 'Zombie' type - but being a Jirina Kudro Human tribal deck, there are likely no Zombie creature cards in the library, so the death trigger would completely whiff. Frontier Warmonger is a Human, matching many creatures in the deck, making the death trigger highly valuable. Additionally, a 7/5 Frontier Warmonger with menace-granting ability is more threatening than a 5/3 Zombie.",
      "action_taken": "Equipped Heirloom Blade to a 2/2 Zombie Token",
      "better_line": "Equip Heirloom Blade to Frontier Warmonger to make it a 7/5 and ensure the death trigger can find a Human creature card from the library",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 314,
      "player": "Haiku4.5",
      "decision_index": 453,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Sonnet4.5 had exactly enough mana (Mountain + Talisman of Indulgence) to cast You Find Some Prisoners to destroy a key artifact. Thran Dynamo on Gem2.5Flash's board provides 3 colorless mana per turn, which is a significant mana advantage. Destroying it would meaningfully slow down Gem2.5Flash's ability to deploy and equip threats.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without casting anything during precombat main phase.",
      "better_line": "Cast You Find Some Prisoners choosing 'Break Their Chains' to destroy Gem2.5Flash's Thran Dynamo, significantly reducing their mana production.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 314,
      "player": "Sonnet4.5",
      "decision_index": 474,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Haiku4.5 is trying to equip Heirloom Blade, but they have no creatures on the battlefield to equip it to. Their graveyard contains all their creatures (Humble Defector, Xathrid Necromancer, Garna, Knight of the White Orchid, Riders of Gavony, Banisher Priest). Equipping requires a target creature you control, so this activation accomplishes nothing and wastes mana. They should have played their Plains from hand instead, or if the equip somehow resolves to nothing, they've wasted the mana that could have been used elsewhere.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to activate Heirloom Blade's Equip ability with no creatures on the battlefield to attach it to.",
      "better_line": "Play Plains from hand as the land drop, then pass since there are no meaningful plays available with no creatures on board.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 314,
      "player": "Haiku4.5",
      "decision_index": 453,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Moved Heirloom Blade from one 2/2 Zombie token to another identical 2/2 Zombie token, wasting 1 mana for zero benefit. Frontier Warmonger (4/4 Human Warrior) was available as an equip target, which would create a 7/5 creature and the death trigger would actually find Human/Warrior creatures in the library.",
      "action_taken": "Equipped Heirloom Blade to a 2/2 Zombie Token",
      "better_line": "Equip Heirloom Blade to Frontier Warmonger, making it a 7/5 with a meaningful death trigger that could find Human or Warrior creatures",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 314,
      "player": "Haiku4.5",
      "decision_index": 453,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Haiku4.5 chose to equip Heirloom Blade before playing their Plains land. Lands should be played before spending mana to maximize available resources. Additionally, Haiku4.5 appears to have no creatures on the battlefield to equip to, making this equip potentially wasteful.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Heirloom Blade's Equip ability before playing Plains from hand",
      "better_line": "Play Plains first, then equip Heirloom Blade (if there's a valid creature target)",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 314,
      "player": "Haiku4.5",
      "decision_index": 453,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Equipped Heirloom Blade to a Zombie token instead of Frontier Warmonger. Heirloom Blade's death trigger searches for a creature sharing a type - Frontier Warmonger is a Human, and this is a Human tribal deck (Jirina Kudro commander), so the death trigger would reliably find another Human. A Zombie token dying would search for Zombies, which this deck has essentially none of.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to equip Heirloom Blade to a 2/2 Zombie Token",
      "better_line": "Equip Heirloom Blade to Frontier Warmonger (4/4 Human Warrior) to make it a 7/5 and ensure the death trigger can find Human creatures from the deck",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 314,
      "player": "Haiku4.5",
      "decision_index": 453,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Sonnet4.5 passed without casting You Find Some Prisoners, which was castable with the untapped Mountain + Talisman of Indulgence. They could have destroyed a key artifact like Thran Dynamo (denying Gem2.5Flash 3 mana) or Darksteel Plate, or used the 'Interrogate' mode for card advantage. With no creatures on board and needing to rebuild, using available mana for value or disruption is important.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting any spells, leaving 2 mana unused.",
      "better_line": "Cast You Find Some Prisoners using 'Break Their Chains' mode to destroy Thran Dynamo (cutting Gem2.5Flash's mana production significantly) or use 'Interrogate Them' mode for potential card advantage from an opponent's library.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 314,
      "player": "Sonnet4.5",
      "decision_index": 474,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Gem2.5Flash cast Serra's Embrace with no creatures on the entire battlefield. There are zero creatures in play - all of Gem2.5Flash's creatures are in the graveyard. The aura requires 'Enchant creature' and will either fizzle (wasting the card and mana) or enchant nothing useful. Serra's Embrace is a powerful card that could have been game-changing once a creature was deployed.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Serra's Embrace ({2}{W}{W}) with no creatures on the battlefield",
      "better_line": "Play Plains for the land drop and pass, holding Hinder as countermagic and saving Serra's Embrace for when a creature is available to enchant",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 326,
      "player": "Gem2.5Flash",
      "decision_index": 491,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem2.5Flash has enough mana to equip either Darksteel Plate or Banshee's Blade (cost {2}) to their creature AND still hold up Hinder ({1}{U}{U}) with remaining mana (Azorius Chancery + Island + Thran Dynamo = 5 mana total). Equipping Darksteel Plate before combat would protect their key creature with indestructible, or Banshee's Blade would grow with combat damage. Instead they passed without equipping anything.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without equipping anything before combat.",
      "better_line": "Equip Darksteel Plate ({2}) to their creature for indestructible protection before combat, still leaving {1}{U}{U} available to hold up Hinder.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 328,
      "player": "Gem2.5Flash",
      "decision_index": 496,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Haiku4.5 at 13 life chose to block only the 2/2 Silverblade Paladin while leaving the 8/9 Elgaud Shieldmate (likely with double strike from Silverblade Paladin's soulbond) completely unblocked. An unblocked 8/9 with double strike deals 16 damage, which is lethal. Even without double strike, 8 damage puts them to 5 life in a very precarious position.",
      "action_taken": "Blocked the 2/2 Silverblade Paladin with a 2/2 Zombie Token, leaving the 8/9 Elgaud Shieldmate unblocked.",
      "better_line": "Multi-block the 8/9 Elgaud Shieldmate with several creatures (e.g., Frontier Warmonger 4/4 + Zombie Token 5/3 + additional Zombies) to absorb or reduce the lethal damage, and let the 2/2 Paladin through for only 2 damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 329,
      "player": "Haiku4.5",
      "decision_index": 503,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Haiku4.5 at 13 life let an 8/9 Elgaud Shieldmate through unblocked (taking 8 damage, dropping to 5) while using two 2/2 Zombie Tokens to block a mere 2/2 Silverblade Paladin. The Frontier Warmonger (4/4) and Zombie Token (5/3) were left unused as blockers against the massive threat.",
      "action_taken": "Blocked only the 2/2 Silverblade Paladin with two 2/2 Zombie Tokens, leaving the 8/9 Elgaud Shieldmate unblocked.",
      "better_line": "Block Elgaud Shieldmate with Frontier Warmonger (4/4) + Zombie Token (5/3) + at least one 2/2 Zombie Token to kill it (combined 11+ power vs 9 toughness), and either chump-block or take the 2 damage from Silverblade Paladin.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 329,
      "player": "Haiku4.5",
      "decision_index": 503,
    }
